{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Standing Ovation feels like a natural next choice because Stages and A Musical Affair reflect my interest in expressive singing and songs from the stage.",
    "Eagles fits my interest in melodic songs and vocal harmonies, while BRINGING BACK THE SUNSHINE connects with the country listening reflected in 747 and Golden."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Motown Anthems and Sounds of Summer offer familiar pop, but that does not give me the theatrical vocals or relaxed, orchestral mood I want right now.",
    "Chicago and Pure 60's feel too broad for this visit; I would rather choose a focused vocal or stage album than a collection spanning many songs and styles."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to assume that enjoying some older melodic music means I want a wide range of older hits.",
    "There is too much emphasis on greatest-hits collections when a familiar era alone does not explain why I would choose an album."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My interest in Stages, A Musical Affair, and the Downton Abbey music makes theatrical singing and orchestral accompaniment especially meaningful to me.",
    "Enjoying smooth harmonies or expressive voices does not make every appealing album an immediate choice: the stage collection takes priority today, and my latest classical selection also suggests an interest in calmer listening."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my taste for melody and strong vocals, but stretched it too broadly into older hits instead of prioritizing stage songs and relaxed orchestral music."
}"}
